# The seventh tooling step's part on `ab` and `try`: a test that failed on both
# sides of an A/B, a commit for the branch's side, `mutate` and `--dependents`
# through `try`, and the words `try` refuses before anything is built. Written
# with the code, and run with `cargo xtask mutate tooling-7-try-ab`.

# ------------------------------------------------ ab: a test failed on both

[break] ab-takes-a-test-that-failed-on-one-side-for-both
rule: A test that failed on one side only is a failure of its round: the two sides must name the same failed tests.
file: xtask/src/ab.rs
in: failed_on_both
find: ids(base) != ids(head)
replace: false
caught-by:
    ab::tests::a_test_that_failed_on_one_side_only_is_still_a_failed_round

[break] ab-takes-a-run-that-broke-for-the-tests-failing
rule: A round is compared past its failed tests only when every failed run failed by its tests.
file: xtask/src/ab.rs
in: failed_on_both
find: if !base.by_tests || !head.by_tests || base.cases.is_empty() || head.cases.is_empty() {
replace: if base.cases.is_empty() || head.cases.is_empty() {
caught-by:
    ab::tests::a_failure_that_the_tests_do_not_explain_is_not_a_test_failing_on_both_sides

[break] ab-takes-a-report-that-names-no-failure-as-the-tests
rule: A report that names no failed test explains nothing of a failed run.
file: xtask/src/ab.rs
in: failure_of
find: let explained = by_tests && !report.failed.is_empty();
replace: let explained = by_tests;
caught-by:
    ab::tests::a_failed_run_names_the_tests_its_report_says_failed

[break] ab-takes-a-run-with-no-report-as-the-tests
rule: A run that wrote no report is not explained by its tests.
file: xtask/src/ab.rs
in: failure_of
find: by_tests: false
replace: by_tests: true
caught-by:
    ab::tests::a_failed_run_names_the_tests_its_report_says_failed

[break] ab-leaves-a-round-with-a-shared-failure-out
rule: A round in which the same tests failed on both sides is compared, without them.
file: xtask/src/ab.rs
in: comparable
find: if failed_on_both(round).is_some() => {
replace: if false => {
caught-by:
    ab::tests::a_test_that_failed_on_both_sides_is_left_out_and_the_others_are_compared

[break] ab-skips-a-test-only-in-the-round-it-failed
rule: A test that failed on both sides in a round is left out of every round, not only that one.
file: xtask/src/ab.rs
in: comparable
find: .filter(|case| !skipped.contains_key(&case.id()))
replace: .filter(|_| true)
caught-by:
    ab::tests::a_test_that_failed_on_both_sides_is_left_out_and_the_others_are_compared

[break] ab-forgets-which-rounds-a-skipped-test-failed-in
rule: A skipped test is named with each round it failed on both sides in.
file: xtask/src/ab.rs
in: comparable
find: .push(index + 1);
replace: .push(1);
occurrence: 1
caught-by:
    ab::tests::a_test_that_failed_on_both_sides_is_left_out_and_the_others_are_compared

[break] ab-swaps-the-sides-messages
rule: A skipped test's message for each side is that side's own.
file: xtask/src/ab.rs
in: comparable
find: base: base.message.clone()
replace: base: head.message.clone()
caught-by:
    ab::tests::a_test_that_failed_on_both_sides_is_left_out_and_the_others_are_compared

[break] ab-lists-a-compared-round-as-failed
rule: A round that is compared past a shared failure is not listed as a failed round.
file: xtask/src/ab.rs
in: failed_rounds
find: if failed_on_both(round).is_some() {
replace: if false {
caught-by:
    ab::tests::a_test_that_failed_on_both_sides_is_left_out_and_the_others_are_compared

[break] ab-names-no-skipped-test-when-there-is-none
rule: With no test failed on both sides there is nothing to say of one.
file: xtask/src/ab.rs
in: skipped_text
find: if skipped.is_empty() {
replace: if false {
caught-by:
    ab::tests::a_test_that_failed_on_both_sides_is_left_out_and_the_others_are_compared

[break] ab-says-the-whole-message-not-its-first-line
rule: A failure is shown by the first line of its message.
file: xtask/src/ab.rs
in: first_line
find: text.lines()
replace: std::iter::once(text)
caught-by:
    ab::tests::a_report_names_each_failed_test_with_the_first_line_of_its_message

[break] ab-takes-an-exit-code-for-the-tests
rule: A run failed by its tests when nextest's exit code says so and its report names a failed test.
